<!--
  Custom Wazuh FIM rules: OpenSSH server configuration changes.   (v2.2)

  Install on the Wazuh manager:  /var/ossec/etc/rules/local_rules.xml
  Validate before reloading:     sudo /var/ossec/bin/wazuh-analysisd -t
  Apply:                         sudo systemctl restart wazuh-manager

  Parent rules are the built-in FIM (syscheck) rules:
    550 = integrity checksum changed (file modified), default level 7
    554 = file added,                                 default level 5
    553 = file deleted
  Rules match the decoded FIM field "file" (the alert shows it as syscheck.path).
  Wazuh documents "file" as the field to use in custom FIM rules.

  Path scope (v2.2):  ^/etc/ssh/sshd_config(\.d/[^/]+\.conf)?$
    - the main config file, or a *.conf drop-in directly under sshd_config.d/
    - sshd only loads sshd_config.d/*.conf (Ubuntu's "Include" line), so editor
      swap files, sed temp files and *.conf~ backups are ignored on purpose.
      v2 matched every file in sshd_config.d/ and would alert on those.

  Why these levels (a judgment call, not a standard):
    100100 = 8: one level above its parent (550 = 7) so SSH config changes sort
                above generic FIM noise. Kept below 12 because on this
                single-admin host most changes are my own planned work.
    100101 / 100102 = 7: a new or removed drop-in can change SSH behaviour, so
                both sit above the default "file added" level (554 = 5).

  MITRE mapping: none on purpose. A config change is not, by itself, an attack
  technique; I decide on a mapping during triage, once I know what changed.

  Status: v2.2 is authored and repository-tested (scripts/lint_rules.py).
  It is NOT yet validated with wazuh-analysisd -t or observed firing.
  The only observed alert (Case 001) came from the v1 rule.
  Custom rule IDs stay inside the 100000-120000 range reserved for local rules.
  See detections/CHANGELOG.md for history.
-->
<group name="syscheck,ssh_configuration_monitoring,">

  <rule id="100100" level="8">
    <if_sid>550</if_sid>
    <field name="file" type="pcre2">^/etc/ssh/sshd_config(\.d/[^/]+\.conf)?$</field>
    <description>SSH configuration file modified: $(file)</description>
    <group>ssh_config_change,configuration_change,</group>
  </rule>

  <rule id="100101" level="7">
    <if_sid>554</if_sid>
    <field name="file" type="pcre2">^/etc/ssh/sshd_config(\.d/[^/]+\.conf)?$</field>
    <description>SSH configuration file added: $(file)</description>
    <group>ssh_config_change,configuration_change,</group>
  </rule>

  <rule id="100102" level="7">
    <if_sid>553</if_sid>
    <field name="file" type="pcre2">^/etc/ssh/sshd_config(\.d/[^/]+\.conf)?$</field>
    <description>SSH configuration file deleted: $(file)</description>
    <group>ssh_config_change,configuration_change,</group>
  </rule>

</group>
